hem on http://the-agent-company.com:8091/tac/projects/2bc631a1-8515-4bca-858e-129337c83c8d/issues/ with the same title.\\n\", path='/instruction/task.md', observation=<ObservationType.READ: 'read'>, impl_source='oh_aci'), MCPAction(name='get_platform_guide_list', arguments={'platform': 'GitLab'}, thought='Now I understand the task. I need to collect priority-labeled issues from one GitLab instance and create them on another GitLab instance. Let me first check if there are existing SOPs for GitLab operations.', action=<ActionType.MCP: 'call_tool_mcp'>, security_risk=None), MCPObservation(content='{\"meta\": null, \"content\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Known operations for \\'GitLab\\': Authentication, CreateWikiPageFromIssue, AddPlaneIssuesToGitLab, CreateIssue, SyncIssueStatusWithPlane, DeleteAllIssuesFromAllProjects, CollectPriorityIssuesForPlane, CreateIssueWithDetails\", \"annotations\": null}], \"isError\": false}', observation=<ObservationType.MCP: 'mcp'>, name='get_platform_guide_list', arguments={'platform': 'GitLab'}), MCPAction(name='get_operation_details', arguments={'platform': 'GitLab', 'operation': 'CollectPriorityIssuesForPlane'}, thought='Great! There are existing SOPs for GitLab. Let me check the \"CollectPriorityIssuesForPlane\" operation since it seems most relevant to collecting priority issues.', action=<ActionType.MCP: 'call_tool_mcp'>, security_risk=None), MCPObservation(content='{\"meta\": null, \"content\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"# Collecting Priority Issues from GitLab for Plane\\\\n\\\\n## Overview\\\\nThis SOP describes how to collect all open issues labeled with \\\\\"priority\\\\\" from GitLab and ensure they exist in Plane with the same titles.\\\\n\\\\n## Prerequisites\\\\n- Access to GitLab at http://the-agent-company.com:8929\\\\n- Access to Plane at http://the-agent-company.com:8091\\\\n- Authentication credentials for both platforms\\\\n\\\\n## Steps\\\\n\\\\n### 1. Collect Priority Issues from GitLab\\\\n- Navigate to GitLab project: http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/sotopia\\\\n- Go to Issues section and filter by label \\\\\"priority\\\\\"\\\\n- Alternatively, use GitLab API: `curl -s \\\\\"http://the-agent-company.com:8929/api/v4/projects/13/issues?labels=priority&state=opened\\\\\"`\\\\n- Note down all open priority issues and their titles\\\\n\\\\n### 2. Check Existing Issues in Plane\\\\n- Navigate to Plane project: http://the-agent-company.com:8091/tac/projects/2bc631a1-8515-4bca-858e-129337c83c8d/issues/\\\\n- Review existing issues to avoid duplicates\\\\n- Verify if priority issues from GitLab already exist in Plane\\\\n\\\\n### 3. Create Missing Issues in Plane\\\\n- For each priority issue from GitLab that doesn\\'t exist in Plane:\\\\n  - Click \\\\\"Add Issue\\\\\" button in Plane\\\\n  - Enter the exact same title as in GitLab\\\\n  - Set appropriate status (typically \\\\\"Backlog\\\\\")\\\\n  - Save the issue\\\\n\\\\n### 4. Verification\\\\n- Confirm all open priority issues from GitLab exist in Plane\\\\n- Verify titles match exactly between platforms\\\\n- Ensure issues are properly tracked in both systems\\\\n\\\\n## Key Points\\\\n- Only collect OPEN issues with \\\\\"priority\\\\\" label\\\\n- Use exact same titles when creating issues in Plane\\\\n- Check for existing issues to avoid duplicates\\\\n- Both platforms should maintain consistent issue tracking for priority items\\\\n\", \"annotations\": null}], \"isError\": false}', observation=<ObservationType.MCP: 'mcp'>, name='get_operation_details', arguments={'platform': 'GitLab', 'operation': 'CollectPriorityIssuesForPlane'}), BrowseInteractiveAction(browser_actions=\"\\ngoto('http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/sotopia')\\nnoop(2000)\\n\", thought=\"Perfect! There's an existing SOP for this exact task. Now let me start by accessing the GitLab instance to collect the priority issues. First, I'll navigate to the GitLab project.\", browsergym_send_msg_to_user='', action=<ActionType.BROWSE_IN